WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.520
Do you want to sit down?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.280
Just look straight ahead.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.400
That's really good. Great.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.000
I like that.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.160
I am an autistic person.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.880
It is obvious when you see me.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.400
I have no voice,
but yearn to say so much.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.120
If you are willing to listen,
I will try to say how I feel.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.200
(STATIC CRACKLING)

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.160
I live in a total blur
of information.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.840
If I have too many people in a room
at one time and one place,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.680
it is too overwhelming for me
to have to process.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.880
I have to jiggle my brain
to make it settle.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.280
It's just how I cope.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.400
Water takes my pain away

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.600
because it allows me to lose myself

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.920
in a place that asks no questions
of my abilities.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.640
Every drop lets me be me.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.440
Before I could communicate
through typing,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.920
I remember that I was frustrated
by people who were kind,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.840
but didn't know my brain
was as good as people who can speak.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.360
I remember being told that I liked
the Teletubbies, which I did,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.240
but I wanted to move on and was
desperate to read books for my age.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.400
Now I have the chance
to speak up for people like me.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.960
I'm speaking from my heart.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.880
Non-verbal people
are pleasing to be around

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.720
because we sense the world in
a deeper way than those who talk.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.080
Because we cannot express
our emotions instantly,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.200
we become deep thinkers.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.720
People-watchers.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.920
We have the same dreams
as everyone else,

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.080
so please don't treat us
differently.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.720
Each of us is a star...

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.640
...eager to be discovered
and named in the atmosphere.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.600
If you acknowledge our abilities,
we can shine brighter.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.280
We have so much to say.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.680
Please hear us.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.440
(APPLAUSE)

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.840
I think we're all better people
for knowing Murray.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.880
He's made such a big difference
to all our lives.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.600
We can actually understand
how deeply he thinks about things.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.800
We've been very privileged
to be part of his life.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.880
His whole experience

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.920
is expressed there in just a few
minutes. It's...

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.840
It's wonderful. Wonderful.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.160
That just sums up everything
about Murray, and it's just lovely

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.920
to be telling us how his world is.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.080
MURRAY: I am happy

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:15.120
that the world

00:03:16.108 --> 00:03:23.320
can see the real me.

